From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] wlan/qcom/wcn6740/wlan: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(wlan/qcom/wcn6740/wlan: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/wlan/qcom/wcn6740/wlan to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
API migrations. Mostly mechanical; entries that change behaviour say so:

  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)
  - del_timer*() renamed timer_delete*() (6.15)
  - from_timer() renamed timer_container_of() (6.16)
  - cfg80211_ops: 6.18 adapters (station/key ops take wireless_dev, radio_idx,
    cfg80211_ap_update, rx_addr) mapping onto the existing handlers; see
    the comment above wlan_hdd_cfg80211_ops
  - cfg80211_new_sta()/cfg80211_del_sta() take the wireless_dev (6.18)
  - dummy NAPI netdev allocated with alloc_netdev_dummy() (6.10)
  - GRO_NORMAL batch state moved to napi->gro (6.15); hrtimer_setup() (6.15)
  - txq_trans_update() takes the netdev; skb_frag_ref() moved to <linux/skbuff_ref.h>
  - sysctl proc_handler takes a const ctl_table (6.11): pktlog uses a local copy
  - qdf_thread_run(): kCFI-safe trampoline instead of casting QDF_STATUS (*)(void *)
    to int (*)(void *), which would trap at runtime under the GKI's kCFI
  - relax unused-but-set-parameter / missing-prototypes / implicit-enum-enum-cast
    to warnings (new clang diagnostics, fatal with CONFIG_WERROR)

35 files.

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * in_irq() -> in_hardirq() (the alias is gone).
  * hex2bin()/hex_to_bin() live in <linux/hex.h>.
